From: VKing <noreply@openwrt.local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: vsc73xx: handle standalone routed marks

A packet routed from an offloaded bridge can retain
offload_fwd_mark when it reaches a standalone DSA egress port. Do not
dereference the absent target
bridge or reuse a bridge VID in that case; keep the target port's
standalone VID.

Signed-off-by: VKing <noreply@openwrt.local>
---
--- a/net/dsa/tag_vsc73xx_8021q.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_vsc73xx_8021q.c
@@ -23,2 +23,2 @@ vsc73xx_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *netdev)
-		if (br_vlan_enabled(br))
+		if (br && br_vlan_enabled(br))
 			return skb;
@@ -26,2 +26,3 @@ vsc73xx_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *netdev)
-		tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge_num);
+		if (br)
+			tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge_num);
 	}
